1
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:04,590
Let's stay up all night chatting, young master.

2
00:00:04,590 --> 00:00:06,810
Tell us all about your youthful troubles.

3
00:00:07,330 --> 00:00:10,450
You're hoping I'll entertain you
while you drink, aren't you?

4
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:13,310
Screw this. I'm going home. Let go.

5
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:17,730
Oh, come on. Tell us everything
that's on your mind.

6
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:20,700
We're such good friends, aren't we?

7
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:22,090
Like hell we are. Let go.

8
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:33,840
Snake

9
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:42,390
What's wrong with you? Hit him back.

10
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:50,590
All right! Right there.

11
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:52,480
Seriously? Again?

12
00:00:58,970 --> 00:01:00,320
Those morons.

13
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,110
They fell.

14
00:01:02,110 --> 00:01:04,070
Does that make it a tie?

15
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:10,860
Nobody knows what they're talking about.

16
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:14,210
They don't get it.

17
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:17,420
They don't even know what they don't know.

18
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:24,180
There's no way they can understand me
when they don't know what they don't know.

19
00:01:25,610 --> 00:01:28,450
Actually, I understand, young master.

20
00:01:28,450 --> 00:01:31,230
After all, 17 is a weird age.

21
00:01:31,230 --> 00:01:33,060
Not quite an adult, but no longer a kid.

22
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:36,850
More.

23
00:01:36,850 --> 00:01:39,170
Sure thing.

24
00:01:39,170 --> 00:01:42,440
Here you go. Whoops.

25
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:46,600
Look at you drink!

26
00:01:49,190 --> 00:01:56,120
Fox, Badger... You're actually laughing
at me on the inside, aren't you?

27
00:01:56,650 --> 00:01:58,890
He's not a fun drunk today.

28
00:01:58,890 --> 00:02:01,210
I'm starting to sober up.

29
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:02,920
We shouldn't have invited him.

30
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:05,050
I can hear you!

31
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:11,310
You think bodyguards like you
have the right to mock me?

32
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:14,690
You serve my dad for a pittance.

33
00:02:14,690 --> 00:02:17,020
Don't you have any pride as warriors?

34
00:02:17,590 --> 00:02:19,970
Please, call us guests.

35
00:02:19,970 --> 00:02:23,450
Even men like us are useful in a fight.

36
00:02:24,610 --> 00:02:26,240
Oh?

37
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,650
You guys actually work sometimes?

38
00:02:28,650 --> 00:02:30,510
I've never seen you do your job, Fox.

39
00:02:30,510 --> 00:02:34,750
This village is so peaceful,
we're bored out of our minds.

40
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:37,120
Draw your sword.

41
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:39,560
I'll test your skills to make sure
you haven't lost your touch.

42
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:55,310
See?

43
00:02:56,690 --> 00:03:00,980
We're your father's guests,
and this is what he pays us to do.

44
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:08,300
Damn it! Just kill me!

45
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:12,830
What should we do, Fox?

46
00:03:13,890 --> 00:03:15,810
That's odd.

47
00:03:15,810 --> 00:03:20,130
We were supposed to have fun drinking
together so Ketil's family would like us.

48
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:24,130
I'm a nobody!

49
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:33,200
In other words, young master,

50
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:38,810
you don't like being treated
like a child by respectable folk.

51
00:03:38,810 --> 00:03:42,150
You guys treat me like one, too.

52
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:45,100
What do you expect?

53
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:47,610
You really are half a man.

54
00:03:47,610 --> 00:03:49,470
But for you to become a real man—

55
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:52,850
Hey, you should be cheering him up.

56
00:03:52,850 --> 00:03:55,710
Quiet, you. I'm going somewhere with this.

57
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:57,400
Just shut up and listen.

58
00:03:58,070 --> 00:03:59,870
You know, young master...

59
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:05,760
Becoming a real man
isn't actually that difficult.

60
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:11,630
All you gotta do is complete a...
rite of passage, I think it's called.

61
00:04:19,370 --> 00:04:21,740
You need to kill a person.

62
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:31,160
Killing a person will make
you feel really confident.

63
00:04:32,180 --> 00:04:34,090
You oughta try it.

64
00:04:36,980 --> 00:04:43,210
Once you know how fragile human bodies are,
you won't be afraid of others anymore.

65
00:04:43,790 --> 00:04:45,850
It'll grow you right up.

66
00:04:46,930 --> 00:04:51,110
It's how all boys become men.

67
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:57,850
B-But... who?

68
00:04:57,850 --> 00:05:01,260
Well, that's obvious.

69
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:05,860
I know of the perfect target for a beginner.

70
00:05:10,650 --> 00:05:14,570
You've even got some right here on this farm.

71
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:26,700
People you're allowed to kill.

72
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:15,530
Boy, I slept well.

73
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:17,990
I'm hungry.

74
00:07:18,570 --> 00:07:22,580
One, two, three, four.

75
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:28,380
There's still a lot more wheat
to harvest today.

76
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:32,590
This farm is way too big.

77
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:42,110
At this rate, we'll have hardly any time
to clear the woods for next spring.

78
00:07:42,510 --> 00:07:46,140
I'd like to get it done in time
for the fall planting season.

79
00:07:47,140 --> 00:07:52,700
But first, we've gotta dig up the roots
and rocks, till the soil, and let it rest.

80
00:07:53,310 --> 00:07:55,820
I wonder if they'll let us
borrow a heavy plow.

81
00:08:05,650 --> 00:08:08,250
Th-Thorfinn, what's wrong?

82
00:08:08,810 --> 00:08:11,790
Are you still asleep? Hey, Thorfinn.

83
00:08:19,210 --> 00:08:21,290
Are you okay?

84
00:08:21,290 --> 00:08:23,510
You were screaming like crazy.

85
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:34,470
What kind of dream
makes a man scream like that?

86
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:38,520
I was dreaming?

87
00:08:39,370 --> 00:08:43,210
I wonder what it was. I can't remember.

88
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:53,660
Go wash your face and let's get
started on our morning tasks.

89
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:59,880
Dreams you forget are better left forgotten.

90
00:09:21,330 --> 00:09:24,530
Good morning. It's a nice morning, isn't it?

91
00:09:24,530 --> 00:09:27,160
Uh, yes. Good morning.

92
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:28,810
Would you like to wash your faces?

93
00:09:28,810 --> 00:09:31,530
Go ahead. I'm already finished.

94
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:33,020
Oh, no. I mean, yes.

95
00:09:33,020 --> 00:09:35,170
Uh, sorry. Take your time.

96
00:09:35,530 --> 00:09:39,790
Washing this face won't make it any better.

97
00:09:40,170 --> 00:09:42,310
Oh, I wouldn't say that.

98
00:09:43,250 --> 00:09:46,060
I think you have a wonderful face.

99
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:53,410
Are you all right? Are you not feeling well?

100
00:09:53,410 --> 00:09:55,440
It's my heart...

101
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:57,440
That's terrible. Does it hurt?

102
00:09:57,440 --> 00:10:01,070
No, I'm fine. I'm not sick or anything.

103
00:10:01,070 --> 00:10:02,430
Then are you injured?

104
00:10:02,430 --> 00:10:06,010
What is this? I feel so uneasy.

105
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:14,760
I must have been dreaming
about something I mustn't forget.

106
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:21,530
My name is Arnheid.

107
00:10:21,530 --> 00:10:23,610
You came here recently, didn't you?

108
00:10:23,610 --> 00:10:25,740
Y-Yes. I'm Einar.

109
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:27,720
I'm from England.

110
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:34,350
England? You speak the language so well,
I thought you were Norse.

111
00:10:34,350 --> 00:10:40,720
Everyone in my village, including me,
is descended from Nords.

112
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:44,060
We all speak English and Norse.

113
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:48,390
Though I'm sure it's hard for a lady like you
to understand me, since my accent is so thick.

114
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:53,180
Oh, that's right. Excuse me.

115
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:56,700
I hadn't mentioned
my status here on the farm.

116
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:06,720
What? Aren't you the master's daughter?

117
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:09,470
No, I'm not.

118
00:11:11,460 --> 00:11:14,330
Like you, I'm a slave.

119
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:17,640
I'm the master's personal attendant.

120
00:11:18,610 --> 00:11:19,550
What?

121
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:27,760
Good morning, gentlemen.

122
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:31,820
Have you slaves gotten together
this morning to plot your escape?

123
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,790
Good morning.

124
00:11:35,010 --> 00:11:36,750
You, what's your name?

125
00:11:37,290 --> 00:11:38,470
Thorfinn.

126
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:42,750
Are you a slave, too? I don't recognize you.

127
00:11:42,750 --> 00:11:46,380
I'm E-Einar. I arrived this summer.

128
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:56,790
Thorfinn and Einar, come with me.

129
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:10,790
We're having a busy morning.

130
00:12:13,270 --> 00:12:16,290
Who are those guys?

131
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:18,620
They've got swords.

132
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:22,290
They aren't respectable folk, are they?

133
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:25,970
They're "guests."

134
00:12:25,970 --> 00:12:29,180
They're the resident
defensive force at the farm.

135
00:12:30,310 --> 00:12:31,740
Basically bodyguards.

136
00:12:34,210 --> 00:12:39,750
Whatever business they've
got with us can't be good.

137
00:12:42,950 --> 00:12:45,720
I think you have a wonderful face.

138
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:51,820
What is it? You're in a good mood, Einar.

139
00:12:51,820 --> 00:12:53,820
Oh, sorry.

140
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:55,820
No problem at all.

141
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:58,830
You seem like a lively one.

142
00:13:25,910 --> 00:13:27,650
Go on, young master.

143
00:13:27,650 --> 00:13:31,450
Make a nice clean cut.

144
00:13:32,310 --> 00:13:35,530
A clean cut? You mean...

145
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:38,990
Very perceptive of you, big man.

146
00:13:38,990 --> 00:13:40,030
What?

147
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:44,500
This ritual will allow the young master
to become a man.

148
00:13:45,570 --> 00:13:46,950
Die for us.

149
00:13:56,730 --> 00:14:00,280
This ritual will allow the young master
to become a man.

150
00:14:00,280 --> 00:14:01,690
Die for us.

151
00:14:06,810 --> 00:14:09,230
Y-You can't be serious!

152
00:14:09,230 --> 00:14:12,900
What have we done to deserve this?

153
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,890
You've done nothing wrong!

154
00:14:14,890 --> 00:14:20,370
But your lives aren't your own.
That's all there is to it.

155
00:14:20,370 --> 00:14:24,970
Your rightful owner is free to do
whatever he pleases with his possessions.

156
00:14:24,970 --> 00:14:29,340
You're a slave that belongs to Olmar's family.

157
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:33,340
He's going to cut you down himself.
You should be honored.

158
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:34,970
Lucky you.

159
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:37,580
Just give up already.

160
00:14:40,710 --> 00:14:44,890
Th-These guys belong to my dad.

161
00:14:44,890 --> 00:14:46,350
They're not mine.

162
00:14:46,880 --> 00:14:49,080
If I cut them down,
I'll have to pay him back for them.

163
00:14:51,110 --> 00:14:53,420
Pathetic, young master.

164
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,860
You've made it this far,
and you're still making excuses?

165
00:14:56,610 --> 00:14:58,780
Are you afraid of your father?

166
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:00,810
Are you afraid to kill?

167
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:02,630
Or are you afraid of both?

168
00:15:02,630 --> 00:15:05,750
Shut up! I'm not scared of anything.

169
00:15:06,060 --> 00:15:09,630
Then do it. Make a nice clean cut.

170
00:15:11,750 --> 00:15:14,070
Thorfinn, run.

171
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:16,880
It'll be fine.

172
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,870
Damn you...

173
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:25,330
What are you doing? Go, Thorfinn!

174
00:15:25,330 --> 00:15:26,950
Tell the master!

175
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:29,450
You can do it, sir!

176
00:15:29,450 --> 00:15:31,310
Your opponent is raring to go!

177
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:36,220
Don't move, shorty.

178
00:15:36,690 --> 00:15:38,430
Shut up and watch.

179
00:15:53,290 --> 00:15:54,790
What a pain.

180
00:15:57,880 --> 00:15:59,610
He can cut me down.

181
00:16:00,970 --> 00:16:02,410
You've got this, sir.

182
00:16:04,970 --> 00:16:07,420
You only need one of us, don't you?

183
00:16:08,350 --> 00:16:10,670
Let him return to work.

184
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,420
He can cut me down.

185
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,240
Ow...

186
00:16:57,010 --> 00:16:58,730
Oh, it's morning.

187
00:17:04,090 --> 00:17:06,220
Hey, Gramps.

188
00:17:07,250 --> 00:17:09,990
Gramps, are you there?

189
00:17:25,090 --> 00:17:29,070
Gramps, where's my breakfast?

190
00:17:29,070 --> 00:17:30,930
Gramps!

191
00:17:30,930 --> 00:17:34,770
You're asking about breakfast
after waking up at this hour?

192
00:17:34,770 --> 00:17:39,470
If you want to eat, help me with the
harvest every once in a while.

193
00:17:39,470 --> 00:17:41,570
No way.

194
00:17:41,570 --> 00:17:44,400
Then I'm not cooking for you.

195
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:47,080
Figure something out yourself.

196
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:49,420
That old fart.

197
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:52,310
I'm not cooking for myself.
What a pain in the butt.

198
00:17:52,750 --> 00:17:55,100
I guess I'll head home.

199
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:13,850
I'll allow Master Olmar to cut me down.

200
00:18:14,390 --> 00:18:17,100
Please let Einar return to work.

201
00:18:18,050 --> 00:18:19,800
We have another busy day.

202
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:25,050
Wh-What did you just say?

203
00:18:37,130 --> 00:18:40,670
Sorry, what's your name again?

204
00:18:41,770 --> 00:18:43,000
It's Thorfinn.

205
00:18:43,820 --> 00:18:45,980
All right, Thorfinn.

206
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:49,840
Do you understand what you just said?

207
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:52,890
Being cut down means dying.

208
00:18:54,310 --> 00:18:55,670
Yes, it certainly does.

209
00:18:58,230 --> 00:19:01,480
You idiot! What are you—

210
00:19:03,170 --> 00:19:06,620
Keep your mouth shut. Stay out of this.

211
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:09,900
Did you hear that, boys?

212
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:13,510
You run into guys like him
every once in a while.

213
00:19:15,060 --> 00:19:20,430
I can't overlook what you just said.

214
00:19:20,430 --> 00:19:26,130
Letting a remark like that slide
reduces the value of our product.

215
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:33,820
Hey, Thorfinn. Do you know
what product we warriors sell?

216
00:19:36,020 --> 00:19:37,030
No.

217
00:19:40,250 --> 00:19:41,480
It's death.

218
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:52,240
Everyone is afraid to die.

219
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:55,260
I can tell you for certain
that everyone fears it.

220
00:19:55,890 --> 00:19:57,790
Look at the young master.

221
00:19:57,790 --> 00:19:59,930
He's even afraid of someone else dying.

222
00:19:59,930 --> 00:20:02,380
Shut up. I'm not s-scared.

223
00:20:02,830 --> 00:20:07,630
You should be.
Death has value because we fear it.

224
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:12,140
Otherwise we wouldn't be able
to use our swords to make a living.

225
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:24,280
You should be scared, too.

226
00:20:25,060 --> 00:20:26,590
Go on. Be afraid.

227
00:20:32,090 --> 00:20:34,540
Aw, man. I'm hungry.

228
00:20:35,320 --> 00:20:37,620
Hey, you punks.

229
00:20:40,570 --> 00:20:42,350
Stop!

230
00:20:44,810 --> 00:20:49,100
Those idiots. They're up to no good again.

231
00:20:50,130 --> 00:20:51,830
Stop!

232
00:20:52,640 --> 00:20:55,890
Damn it! You monsters!

233
00:20:57,650 --> 00:20:58,670
Come on.

234
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:01,230
Beg for your life.

235
00:21:01,710 --> 00:21:04,970
Don't hide your true feelings, Thorfinn.

236
00:21:11,050 --> 00:21:12,300
Ouch.

237
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:19,950
If you don't hurry up, your tiny
little body will end up even smaller.

238
00:21:27,210 --> 00:21:33,090
Huh, he didn't even blink. Impressive.

239
00:21:34,210 --> 00:21:37,980
Isn't that one of the master's slaves?

240
00:21:43,560 --> 00:21:48,870
Why do we have to fear death?

241
00:21:53,510 --> 00:21:56,090
Do we live because we don't want to die?

242
00:21:59,110 --> 00:22:04,140
Does anything good come from being alive?

243
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:12,040
Not for me.

244
00:22:16,950 --> 00:22:23,020
Not a single good thing has
happened to me in my entire life.

245
00:22:44,470 --> 00:22:46,070
Your eye is next.

246
00:22:49,700 --> 00:22:50,860
Show me that you're afraid.

247
00:22:51,300 --> 00:22:52,460
Don't, Fox!

248
00:22:58,840 --> 00:23:00,540
S-Snake...

249
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:14,060
Aw, man. He's in rough shape.

250
00:23:17,530 --> 00:23:22,810
B-Boss, welcome back.
Wh-Wh-When did you get here?

251
00:23:22,810 --> 00:23:23,620
Fox.

252
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:24,730
Yes, sir.

253
00:23:26,250 --> 00:23:27,250
Come closer.

254
00:23:27,250 --> 00:23:28,570
Y-Yes, sir.

255
00:23:45,290 --> 00:23:46,290
Badger.

256
00:23:46,290 --> 00:23:47,690
Yes, sir!

257
00:23:52,450 --> 00:23:53,750
Explain.

258
00:25:36,670 --> 00:25:39,760
Awakening

259
00:25:37,800 --> 00:25:39,070
"Awakening."
